  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Chronic Crisis - Venezuela Country Operational Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Country Operational Plan
Venezuela has been facing a prolonged socio-political and economic crisis that has negatively impacted social and health indicators. Since 2016, the country has been impacted by a series of public health concerns ranging from re-emerging disease outbreaks to reduced availability of essential health services due to the shortages of health commodities, migration of health personnel, and the general economic situation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">30.000 people, Female 80%, Male 20%</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Most vulnerable families are still facing critical difficulties to access primary health care, food, essential supplies, and protection services due to their high costs. Access to sexual and reproductive health services is extremely limited with Venezuela facing steeper declines in key indicators such as antenatal care and skilled birth attendance than the average within the region in recent years. Furthermore, the prolonged COVID-19 crisis has further accentuated health sector shortages, including human, financial and material resources, increases in maternal and infant mortality, as well as issues related to mental health and domestic and intra-familiar violence, reducing the activities to the public program related to Sexual and Reproductive Health.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Primary health care services with a focus on Sexual and Reproductive Health services (SRH) will be provided through health days, which will include medical consultations, mental health and psychosocial support activities, vital signs monitoring, biometric values, such as weight and height, health promotion and disease prevention provision of sexual reproductive health services (prenatal control, postnatal control, provision of contraceptive methods, care of sexually transmitted infections, early diagnosis of uterine cancer and breast cancer).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing integrated primary health care services with a community-based approach to maternal and child health in the states of Delta Amacuro, Amazonas, Apure, Barinas, Portuguesa, and Gu&#xe1;rico</narrative>
  </description>
